concept what_is_wcl {
  name = "What WCL Is"
  summary = "A typed configuration & schema language: declare types, compose a document, validate and evaluate it."
  related = [fields, blocks]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p <<DOC
      WCL is a typed configuration & schema language: you declare record types, compose a document
      of block instances, and the toolchain validates and evaluates it.
    DOC
    p <<DOC
      A WCL document is built from two structural pieces —
      [fields](concept_fields) that bind names to values and [blocks](concept_blocks) that group and
      nest them — and a schema (written with decorators) that says which blocks and fields are
      legal. `wcl check` validates a document against that schema, and `wcl eval` resolves it to
      plain data.
    DOC
    p <<DOC
      Where most config formats stop at untyped key/value data, WCL adds a type system (numbers with
      widths, strings with encodings, unions, interfaces, references), first-class functions, and a
      document model that gathers and validates structured blocks — so a configuration can carry its
      own schema and be checked before anything consumes it.
    DOC
  }
}
